WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.550
Step five shows the
reader's rules at work.

2
00:00:02.550 --> 00:00:06.386
You build a reader for the inventory
task, with the fixture invoker

3
00:00:06.386 --> 00:00:10.500
standing in for the network, and ask it
for a call the task doesn't declare.

4
00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:12.582
It refuses before anything is sent,

5
00:00:12.582 --> 00:00:16.388
and tells you to add the call to
the call list with its permission.

6
00:00:16.388 --> 00:00:21.343
Then you ask for the cloud G C C in
capitals, and it refuses that too:

7
00:00:21.343 --> 00:00:26.487
the cloud names are global, gcc,
gcchigh and dod, and it never guesses.

8
00:00:26.487 --> 00:00:29.975
Step six reads the hand-off
to the Data Platform plan.

9
00:00:29.975 --> 00:00:35.855
Two accounts go by their SQL Server
service principal names, svc sqlprod and

10
00:00:35.855 --> 00:00:41.112
the group managed account gmsa sql, and
one, svc ldapbind, goes by its name.

11
00:00:41.112 --> 00:00:46.149
Step seven runs every test: five
hundred thirteen pass, none fail.

12
00:00:46.149 --> 00:00:48.050
Then delete the output folder.
